9. Freeze Process (Camunda Trigger)

Instead of cron job:

Camunda triggers freeze.

26th
|
Stop hedge supply
|
Freeze supply snapshot
|
Switch inventory view


---

Step 1 — Stop Supply

Camunda updates cycle:

UPDATE CLO_REPLENISHMENT_CYCLE
SET CYCLE_STATUS='REQUEST_STOPPED'
WHERE cycle_id=:cycle_id;

CLO API rejects new hedges.


---

Step 2 — Freeze Hedge Pool

INSERT INTO CLO_CYCLE_HEDGE_POOL
(
cycle_id,
hedge_id,
frozen_supply_amt
)
SELECT
:cycle_id,
hedge_id,
reqd_hedge_amt
FROM CLO_HEDGE
WHERE created_cycle_id=:cycle_id;


---

Step 3 — Freeze Loan Inventory

Camunda switches view.

CLO_LOAN_INVENTORY_VIEW
→ monthly


---

10. Allocation Queries

Allocation per program

SELECT
program_id,
SUM(amount) allocation
FROM CLO_HEDGE_ALLOCATIONS
GROUP BY program_id;


---

Hedge utilization

SELECT
p.hedge_id,
p.frozen_supply_amt,
NVL(SUM(a.amount),0) used_amt,
p.frozen_supply_amt - NVL(SUM(a.amount),0) remaining
FROM CLO_CYCLE_HEDGE_POOL p
LEFT JOIN CLO_HEDGE_ALLOCATIONS a
ON p.hedge_id=a.hedge_id
GROUP BY
p.hedge_id,
p.frozen_supply_amt;


